course: dictionary
lesson: 3398
title: Experimental: tested and new
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Experimental comes from experiment, a test you do to find something out. A scientist writes down what happens and uses those notes as «experimental results».
explain: The second meaning is new and still being tested, not yet proved to work. In the news you may read that «using animal organs is very new, rare and still experimental». That means doctors are still checking whether it is safe and works.
explain: The third meaning is about art, music or writing that tries new, unusual ways. Look at the clues around the word to see which meaning fits: is it a test, a medicine, or a daring new style?
fact: Experimental means to do with experiments, or new and still being tested.
fact: «Experimental results» are the results of a test you did to find something out.
fact: «An experimental drug» is a medicine that is new and not yet proved to work.
fact: In art and music, experimental means unusual or daring, trying new ways.
fact: A good check is to swap in «new and still being tested» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The scientists wrote down their experimental results.» What does experimental mean here? | *Found by doing a test | Loud and noisy | Something new that nobody has tried | Very old
exercise: «Doctors are giving an experimental medicine, but it has not been proved to work yet.» What does experimental mean? | Made of sugar only | *New and still being tested | Very old and well known | Fully proved and used by everyone
exercise: Ms Lee says her painting is experimental. What does it suggest? | *Unusual and daring, trying new ways | Exactly like every other painting | Very wet and cold | Made in a test tube
test:
test: Ruby wrote down what happened in her own science test. Why are these notes called experimental? | *Because they came from a test to find something out | Because they are a made-up story | Because they are unclear | Because they are very old
test: «The engineers flew an experimental plane over the lake.» What does experimental mean? | *New and still being tested | Old and rusty | Full of water | Painted bright red
exam: «An experimental medicine» is closest in meaning to which words? | Tasty and sweet | Famous and loved | Ancient and cracked | *Still being tested
